*html
	<div class="ct-brandrow"><span class="ct-logo"></span><span class="ct-wordmark">Clearer Thinking</span></div>
	<div class="ct-hero-img" role="img" aria-label="Drawing of an owl in glasses writing at a desk, with a to-do list, a clock, books and a coffee mug"></div>
	<p class="ct-eyebrow">Free live workshop with Spencer Greenberg</p>
	<h1 class="ct-title ct-hero">{workshopTitle}</h1>
	<p class="ct-sub">{workshopSubtitle}</p>

*component
	*classes: ct-facts
	*html
		<p><b>When:</b> {whenText}</p>
		<p><b>Where:</b> Online, live on Zoom. We'll email you the link to join.</p>
		<p><b>Format:</b> Hands-on. A little theory, mostly exercises, including breakout rooms.</p>
		<p><b>Cost:</b> Free</p>
		<p class="ct-skip"><a href="?src={src}&jump=form">Sign up now</a></p>

*html
	<p>You know the project. The side business, the book, the job application, the course you paid for, the report that was due last week. You care about it. You even set time aside for it. And somehow that time goes to email, chores, or your phone instead. Then comes the guilt, and the guilt makes the next start harder still.</p>
	<p>If that sounds familiar, you're not lazy and you're not alone. Research on procrastination suggests it has less to do with laziness than with how we react to tasks that feel unclear, unpleasant, or uncertain. That's good news, because reactions like that can be changed with the right techniques.</p>
	<p>This workshop is about those techniques, and about putting them to work on your own project during the session, so you leave having already started.</p>
	<h2 class="ct-h2">What you'll get</h2>
	<ul class="ct-list">
		<li><b>Why you put things off.</b> What the research literature and Clearer Thinking's own studies show about the causes of procrastination, so you can spot the ones behind your own delays.</li>
		<li><b>Techniques that fit the cause.</b> Different reasons for delay call for different fixes. You'll learn which ones match your situation.</li>
		<li><b>Practice, not just theory.</b> Most of the hour is exercises you do on a real project of yours, including breakout rooms where you'll meet and work with other participants.</li>
		<li><b>Two Q&A sessions.</b> Ask Spencer anything you want, about procrastination or otherwise.</li>
	</ul>

*component
	*classes: ct-callout
	*html
		<p><b>Book giveaway, live attendees only.</b> During the session we'll give away a signed copy of the book <i>12 Levers</i>. Only people attending live are eligible.</p>

*component
	*classes: ct-callout ct-pair
	*html
		<p><b>Optional: an accountability partner.</b> When you sign up, you can choose to be paired with another participant after the workshop, so you can keep each other on track with your projects.</p>
		<p>Each month for six months, we'll introduce you by email to a new partner. We only make the introductions; the rest is up to the two of you. The only thing we share with your partner is your email address. It's entirely optional.</p>

*html
	<h2 class="ct-h2">Who it's for</h2>

Anyone with a personal or professional project that keeps slipping: students, employees, founders, writers, and anyone who knows what they want to work on and still struggles to start. Bring a project in mind; you'll be working on it during the session.

*html
	<h2 class="ct-h2">Who's leading it</h2>

*component
	*classes: ct-bio
	*html
		<div class="ct-bio-row">
			<span class="ct-avatar" role="img" aria-label="Photo of Spencer Greenberg"></span>
			<p class="ct-name"><b>{facilitatorName}</b></p>
			<p class="ct-role">{facilitatorLine}</p>
			<p class="ct-bio-para">Spencer Greenberg is a mathematician and entrepreneur who has kept several long-running projects moving at once, for years. He founded Clearer Thinking, which publishes free, research-based tools, studies and articles on decision-making and psychology; Positly, a platform for recruiting research participants; GuidedTrack, the platform behind Clearer Thinking's interactive tools (and this sign-up page); and PersonalityMap, a tool for exploring how human traits relate to one another. He also hosts the Clearer Thinking podcast and has published essays and videos on social media consistently for years. This workshop draws on the research literature on procrastination, Clearer Thinking's own research on the topic, and what Spencer has learned getting his own projects done.</p>
		</div>

*html
	<h2 class="ct-h2">Can't make it live?</h2>

Sign up anyway: the session will be recorded, and we'll send the recording to everyone who registered. But this is a hands-on workshop, so most of its value comes from being there live: the exercises, the breakout rooms, the Q&A, and the book giveaway.

Sign up below. You'll get a confirmation email right away, and the link to join before the session.

*html
	<div id="ct-signup"></div>

*button: Sign up

