				<p>That email address doesn't look complete (it needs an @ and a dot after it). Please check it and try again.</p>

	*html
		<div class="ct-brandrow"><span class="ct-logo"></span><span class="ct-wordmark">Clearer Thinking</span></div>
		<h1 class="ct-title">Where should we send the link to join?</h1>

	*question: Email address
		*type: text
		*placeholder: you@example.com
		*save: signupEmail

	*question: First name (optional)
		*type: text
		*blank
		*placeholder: Your first name
		*save: signupFirstName

	*question: Would you like an accountability partner after the workshop?
		*tip: Optional and free. Each month for six months, we'll introduce you by email to a new participant, so you can keep each other on track. We only share your email address, nothing else.
		*save: accountabilityPair
		Yes, pair me with someone
		No, thanks

	*question: What's one project you keep putting off? (optional)
		*type: paragraph
		*blank
		*placeholder: e.g., Finishing my portfolio, starting a newsletter, my thesis
		*tip: You'll work on it during the session. If you opted in above, it also helps us pair you well.
		*save: projectToWorkOn

	*question: Anything you'd like to ask Spencer in the Q&A? (optional)
		*type: paragraph
		*blank
		*placeholder: Any question, about procrastination or anything else
		*save: questionForSession

	*button: Confirm sign up

-- Light check that the address can receive mail: exactly one @ with text on both sides, no
-- spaces, and a dot inside the DOMAIN with at least two characters after it. The dot is looked
-- for in the domain alone because text.find only returns the FIRST match (first.last@... is valid).
>> signupEmail = signupEmail.clean
>> emailLooksWrong = 0
>> atPosition = signupEmail.find("@")
>> spacePosition = signupEmail.find(" ")
*if: not atPosition
	>> emailLooksWrong = 1
*if: spacePosition
	>> emailLooksWrong = 1
*if: atPosition
	*if: atPosition < 2
		>> emailLooksWrong = 1
	*if: atPosition > 1
		>> emailParts = signupEmail.split("@")
		>> emailPartCount = emailParts.size
		*if: not (emailPartCount = 2)
			>> emailLooksWrong = 1
		*if: emailPartCount = 2
			>> emailDomain = emailParts[2]
			>> domainDot = emailDomain.find(".")
			>> domainSize = emailDomain.size
			*if: not domainDot
				>> emailLooksWrong = 1
			*if: domainDot
				*if: domainDot < 2
					>> emailLooksWrong = 1
				*if: domainDot > domainSize - 2
					>> emailLooksWrong = 1
*if: emailLooksWrong = 1
	*goto: signupForm

>> signedUpAt = calendar::now

-- 1 when the registrant wants an accountability partner (filter the export on this).
>> accountabilityOptIn = 0
*if: accountabilityPair = "Yes, pair me with someone"
	>> accountabilityOptIn = 1

